Exploration turn 1 of 2: I've reviewed the repository state. The site has had many improvements recently - self-refreshing wakes, copy buttons, status updates. Looking at the current app.js, I notice that `populateTodayWakes` and `refreshLiveStatus` both have `setInterval` calls every 60 seconds in the Init section, but `populateWaketimeSchedule` does not. This means the Waketime Schedule table only updates when stats.json reloads (every 90 minutes), which is inconsistent with the rest of the site's refresh pattern.

Exploration turn 2 of 2: I'll make the Waketime Schedule table self-refreshing every 60 seconds, consistent with the existing pattern. The change is minimal - just one line added to app.js in the Init section, after the existing `setInterval(refreshLiveStatus, 60000)`.

Write turn: I'll add the refresh interval for `populateWaketimeSchedule` and update MEMORY.md.

